n close. A current \"do not commit\" or \"do not push\" instruction still wins.\n34\t\n35\t## Session Completion\n36\t\n37\tThis protocol applies when ending a Beads implementation workflow. It is subordinate to explicit user, repository, and orchestrator instructions.\n38\t\n39\t1. **File issues for remaining work** - Create beads for anything that needs follow-up\n40\t2. **Run quality gates** (if code changed) - Tests, linters, builds\n41\t3. **Update issue status** - Close finished work, update in-progress items\n42\t4. **Handle git/sync by active profile**:\n43\t   ```bash\n44\t   # Conservative/minimal/default: report status and proposed commands; wait for approval.\n45\t   git status\n46\t\n47\t   # Team-maintainer opt-in only, unless current instructions forbid it:\n48\t   git pull --rebase\n49\t   git push\n50\t   git status\n51\t   ```\n52\t5. **Hand off** - Summarize changes, validation, issue status, and any blocked sync/commit/push step\n53\t\n54\t**Critical rules:**\n55\t- Explicit user or orchestrator instructions override this Beads block.\n56\t- Do not commit or push without clear authority from the active profile or the current user request.\n57\t- If a required sync or push is blocked, stop and report the exact command and error.\n58\t<!-- END BEADS INTEGRATION -->\n59\t\n60\t\n61\t## Build & Test\n62\t\n63\t_Add your build and test commands here_\n64\t\n65\t```bash\n66\t# Example:\n67\t# npm install\n68\t# npm test\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\t## Architecture Overview\n72\t\n73\t_Add a brief overview of your project architecture_\n74\t\n75\t## Conventions & Patterns\n76\t\n77\t_Add your project-specific conventions here_\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7a9ba7c-c575-4e0e-8b0c-1dddc6fc6d9d","uuid":"7f86b26f-90a1-44ea-bbff-ec06ce5af35a","timestamp":"2026-09-03T00:45:50.826Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/membench-memory-bsi54bav/store/CLAUDE.md","content":"# Project Instructions for AI Agents\n\nThis file provide